    "legend": "The anterior pituitary neuroendocrine tumour cells are arranged in diffuse sheets or lobules, and they are variably positive for ACTH. In contrast, rosette- or follicle-forming cuboidal or columnar primitive Rathke pouch epithelium and blastemal undifferentiated cells are negative for ACTH.",
